W44-38 chunk A — extend try_dct64 default from `effort >= 7` to `effort >= 6`
========================================================================

Status: [BLOCKED by cost-model wedge] — change NOT shipped. Source reverted.

Hostname: $(hostname) (water-cooled 7950X)
Date: 2026-05-19
Git rev (workspace `~/work/zen/jxl-encoder--w44-38-dct64-hint-e6`):
  main@origin = 145b5595 (W44-37 investigation commit)
Sibling workspace baseline diff: zero (reverted via `jj restore`)

# What was tried

Lowered `EffortProfile::lossy` default `try_dct64: effort >= 7` →
`effort >= 6` in `jxl-encoder/src/effort.rs:778`. Rationale:
libjxl `enc_ac_strategy.cc:855` early-returns from `ProcessRectACS` at
`speed_tier > kHare` (= our e4); for speed_tier <= kHare (= our e5+)
the merge stage evaluates the DCT64X32/DCT32X64 entries in
`kTransformsForMerge` (`enc_ac_strategy.cc:917-918`).
`encoding_speed_tier_max_limit` is checked in `FindBest8x8Transform`
(`:580`), NOT in the merge loop — only `decoding_speed_tier_max_limit`
gates the merge entries. So libjxl evaluates DCT64 at e5+; our
`effort >= 7` gate is 2 effort levels MORE conservative than libjxl.

# What happened

(a) **codec_wiki e6 d=4.0 (the target wedge cell)**:
    AC strategy distribution shifted EXACTLY to cjxl parity
    (Dct64 area_pct: 0.0 → 55.19 = matches cjxl's 55.19 area_pct).
    But bytes REGRESSED: 76795 → 77048 (+253 bytes, +0.34pp delta vs cjxl,
    went from +3.20% to +3.54%). SSIM2 regressed: 79.58 → 79.09 (-0.50).
    Butteraugli unchanged. Status: still OPEN.

    Root cause: the cost-model wedge documented in
    `~/.claude/projects/-home-lilith-work-zen-jxl-encoder/memory/dropped_optimizations_for_parity_2026-05-15.md`
    item #3 — our `entropy_mul` for DCT64x64/DCT64x32/DCT32x64 are lifted
    above libjxl reference values to compensate for missing
    `kAvoidEntropyOfTransforms` + X-channel multi-block weight + kFavor2X2
    coverage. With our lifted muls, evaluating libjxl-faithful DCT64 picks
    spends more bits per block than ours would.

(b) **Photo regressions at e6, d>=2.0** (`benchmarks/w44_38_try_dct64_e6_photos_2026-05-19.tsv`):
    All 12 cells remain status FIXED, but SSIM2 drops are concerning:
    - 1418519.png d=3.0: ssim2 -1.31 (was -0.77), bytes -1.73% (was +1.17%)
    - 1418519.png d=4.0: ssim2 -1.54 (was -1.07), bytes -1.70% (was +0.61%)
    - 1531677.png d=4.0: ssim2 -1.24 (was -1.16), bytes -1.07% (was +2.66%)
    - 1025469.png d=4.0: ssim2 -0.51 (was -0.33), bytes -0.64% (was +2.31%)
    Photos d=1.0: byte-identical (small+low-d gate keeps try_dct64=false,
    consistent with e7 behaviour).

# Why this is a hard wall, not just tuning noise

The bytes ratio at codec_wiki went the WRONG direction even with
strategy distribution at perfect parity. This means the DCT64 blocks
that ARE picked carry more bits than libjxl's would under the same
strategy. The encoder is not just over-picking — it's spending more
per block.

`dropped_optimizations_for_parity_2026-05-15.md` lists this as the
top-3 reason we ship entropy_mul values lifted above the libjxl ref:
    "1-3% file size, mixed quality direction. The wedge is per-image:
     some images want our higher mul (less over-pick of large
     transforms), some want libjxl's lower mul. Single global value
     can't satisfy both."

# Next attempt — what's needed before this gate is safe to lower

Per `dropped_optimizations_for_parity_2026-05-15.md` item #3:

  "How to re-enable libjxl-faithful values: drop everything to
   `EntropyMulTable::reference()` from `forks/cost.rs:530-560`. Then either:
   1. Implement the missing libjxl counterweights (X-channel multi-block
      weight, kAvoidEntropyOfTransforms penalty, kFavor2X2 on more
      strategies). Then libjxl muls work directly.
   2. Per-image cost-model gating (e.g. screenshot discriminator pattern).
   3. Per-region adaptive entropy_mul.
   4. Accept the per-image wedge: ship libjxl muls, tolerate 1-3%
      per-image variance in either direction."

Chunk A as specified in `codec_wiki_wedge_investigation_2026-05-19` is
blocked on option (1) or (3). Option (4) is a no-go because of the
photo SSIM2 regressions (-1.3 to -1.5 on 1418519 d=3/4) — these are
visible quality losses on photos to chase a screenshot wedge cell that
isn't actually closed.

A NARROWER chunk-A variant could be: enable e6 `try_dct64` ONLY when
the smooth_photo_dct64 discriminator says "screenshot-class content"
(median(mask1x1) > 95 per the W44-35 calibration), with the existing
small+low-d gate continuing to apply. That would localise the change
to genuine screenshot inputs and could be A/B tested without photo
collateral damage. The discriminator already exists in
`api::detect_smooth_photo_for_dct64_from_layout` — but it's a
SMOOTH-photo discriminator, not a screenshot one. Would need a
separate W44-38b chunk to build the screenshot discriminator.

